<title>USA: Goodyear to close Jamaica factory.</title>
<headline>Goodyear to close Jamaica factory.</headline>
<dateline>AKRON, Ohio 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Co said on Friday that Goodyear Jamaica Ltd is closing its Morant Bay facility immediately.</p>
<p>The plant closing affects 148 salary and hourly workers, Goodyear said.</p>
<p>Displaced workers may be eligible for benefits under Jamaican law and under the company's employee benefit plans, Goodyear said.</p>
<p>Goodyear said it plans to maintain a strong sales presence in Jamaica.  </p>
<p>Goodyear said the plant's small size and lower cost competition and the company's ability to service this market from more efficient sources led to the decision.</p>
<p>Goodyear Jamaica has not decided what to do with the facility, but it is in talks with officials about future potential uses for the facility, the company said.</p>
</text>
